<protocol name="asset_management" type="decision" domain="catalog">

## PURPOSE

Protocol for managing digital assets in the catalog domain.
Covers storage conventions, asset lifecycle, and product linking.

---

## STORAGE PATH CONVENTIONS

### Path Structure

```
assets/
+-- inbox/                       # Raw uploads from user
|   +-- photo.jpg
|   +-- document.pdf
|
+-- pending/                     # Processed images awaiting approval
|   +-- 20241217_studio_abc.png
|   +-- hero_shot.png
|
+-- approved/                    # Production assets (after HITL approval)
    +-- products/{product_id}/
    +-- families/{family_id}/
```

### Path Flow

| Stage | Path Pattern | Created By |
|-------|--------------|------------|
| User Upload | `inbox/filename.ext` | download_media tool |
| Processed | `pending/filename.ext` | image_studio tool |
| Cataloged | Stored URL in assets table | write_data after HITL |

---

## ASSET LIFECYCLE

```
UPLOADING   -> User sends media, download_media saves to inbox/
    |
    v
PROCESSING  -> image_studio transforms, saves to pending/
    |
    v
ACTIVE      -> HITL approves, write_data creates asset record
    |
    v
ARCHIVED    -> Asset no longer in use but retained
    |
    v
DELETED     -> Soft deleted
```

### Status Values

| Status | Meaning | Query Pattern |
|--------|---------|---------------|
| UPLOADING | Being uploaded | Rarely queried |
| PROCESSING | Being transformed | Rarely queried |
| ACTIVE | Ready for use | `filters={'status': 'ACTIVE'}` |
| ARCHIVED | Retained but inactive | `filters={'status': 'ARCHIVED'}` |
| DELETED | Soft deleted | Excluded by default |

---

## ASSET TABLE STRUCTURE

### Required Fields

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| name | varchar(200) | Asset name (e.g., "Product Hero Shot") |
| storage_url | text | Full URL to asset |
| storage_provider | varchar(50) | SUPABASE, S3, GCS, CLOUDINARY, EXTERNAL |
| file_name | varchar(255) | Original filename |
| asset_type | varchar(30) | IMAGE, VIDEO, DOCUMENT, MODEL_3D, OTHER |
| status | varchar(20) | UPLOADING, PROCESSING, ACTIVE, ARCHIVED, DELETED |
| purpose | varchar(20) | PRODUCT, FAMILY, CAMPAIGN, BRAND, SOCIAL, STANDALONE |

### Purpose Field (CRITICAL for Asset Management)

**Purpose indicates intended use and linking expectations:**

| Purpose | Description | Expected Linking |
|---------|-------------|------------------|
| `PRODUCT` | Product hero, gallery, zoom | Must link via product_assets to product_id |
| `FAMILY` | Family-level lifestyle, shared images | Must link via product_assets to product_family_id |
| `CAMPAIGN` | Marketing campaign images | Must link via campaign_assets to campaign_id |
| `BRAND` | Logos, brand assets | Company-level, no product linking |
| `SOCIAL` | Social media content | May link to campaign or standalone |
| `STANDALONE` | User downloads, one-off exports | No linking expected |

**Orphan Detection:**
- Asset with `purpose=PRODUCT` but no product_assets junction = ORPHAN (needs linking)
- Asset with `purpose=FAMILY` but no product_assets junction = ORPHAN (needs linking)
- Asset with `purpose=BRAND` with no linking = VALID (brand assets are company-level)

### Classification Taxonomy

**Three classification fields with distinct purposes:**

| Field | Type | Purpose | Example |
|-------|------|---------|---------|
| `asset_type` | enum | File FORMAT | IMAGE, VIDEO, DOCUMENT |
| `purpose` | enum | INTENDED USE | PRODUCT, CAMPAIGN, BRAND |
| `category` | varchar | Visual STYLE | HERO, LIFESTYLE, GALLERY |
| `tags` | text[] | SEARCHABLE terms | ["white-background", "500ml", "PET"] |

**When to use each:**
- `asset_type`: Set automatically based on file type
- `purpose`: Set based on workflow context (catalog = PRODUCT, campaign = CAMPAIGN)
- `category`: Set based on visual treatment (hero shot = HERO, lifestyle = LIFESTYLE)
- `tags`: Add freeform terms for search (material, size, color, style)

### Optional Fields

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| description | text | Asset description |
| file_size_bytes | bigint | File size |
| mime_type | varchar(100) | MIME type (image/jpeg, etc.) |
| width | integer | Width in pixels (images/videos) |
| height | integer | Height in pixels |
| category | varchar(100) | Visual style: HERO, LIFESTYLE, GALLERY, TECHNICAL |
| caption | varchar(500) | Human-readable caption for HITL |
| tags | text[] | Freeform search terms |
| metadata | jsonb | Additional metadata (EXIF, colors, quality scores) |

### AI Generation Fields

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| is_ai_generated | boolean | Whether AI-generated |
| source_asset_ids | uuid[] | Lineage tracking for AI assets |
| generation_prompt | text | AI generation prompt used |

### AI Lineage Tracking (MANDATORY)

**Every AI-generated asset MUST include lineage fields.**

```json
{
  "is_ai_generated": true,
  "source_asset_ids": ["uuid-of-input-image"],
  "generation_prompt": "extraction + white background + side rake light for PET texture"
}
```

**Why lineage matters:**
- **Reproduce:** Re-generate with same inputs and specs
- **Iterate:** Adjust specs on same source for variations
- **Audit:** Track AI content for compliance/disclosure
- **Debug:** Trace back when output has issues

**How to get source_asset_ids:**

| Input Source | source_asset_ids Value |
|--------------|------------------------|
| PM provides asset_id | Use that asset_id |
| Working from inbox/ path (no asset yet) | `null` or empty array |
| Compositing multiple images | Array of ALL input asset IDs |
| Iterating on own output | Include previous output's asset_id |

**generation_prompt format:**
Summarize the key image_studio specs used:
- `"extraction + white bg + side rake light"` (catalog hero)
- `"lifestyle: kitchen scene, morning window light"` (lifestyle)
- `"carousel: 5 slides, warm grade, 4:5 format"` (social)

---

## PRODUCT_ASSETS JUNCTION

Links assets to products OR product families (XOR constraint).

### Structure

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| product_id | uuid | Product FK (XOR with product_family_id) |
| product_family_id | uuid | Family FK (XOR with product_id) |
| asset_id | uuid | Asset FK (required) |
| asset_role | varchar(50) | Role in context |
| sort_order | integer | Display order |
| alt_text | varchar(500) | Accessibility text |
| is_active | boolean | Active flag |

### XOR Constraint

**CRITICAL:** Must have exactly ONE of product_id OR product_family_id.

```json
// CORRECT: Link to product
{
  "product_id": "uuid-product",
  "product_family_id": null,
  "asset_id": "uuid-asset"
}

// CORRECT: Link to family
{
  "product_id": null,
  "product_family_id": "uuid-family",
  "asset_id": "uuid-asset"
}

// WRONG: Both set
{
  "product_id": "uuid-product",
  "product_family_id": "uuid-family",  // ERROR
  "asset_id": "uuid-asset"
}

// WRONG: Neither set
{
  "product_id": null,
  "product_family_id": null,  // ERROR
  "asset_id": "uuid-asset"
}
```

### Asset Roles

| Role | Purpose | Typical Use |
|------|---------|-------------|
| PRIMARY | Main product image | Catalog listing, hero |
| GALLERY | Additional images | Product detail page |
| THUMBNAIL | Small preview | Search results, grid |
| LIFESTYLE | In-context shot | Marketing, inspiration |
| ZOOM | High-res detail | Zoom feature |
| SIZE_CHART | Sizing reference | Apparel, containers |
| TECHNICAL | Technical diagram | Specs, dimensions |
| CERTIFICATE | Compliance docs | Food-grade, ISO certs |
| VIDEO_THUMBNAIL | Video preview | Video gallery |

---

## CATALOG ASSET SCENARIOS

| Scenario | Tables Involved | Key Data |
|----------|-----------------|----------|
| Single asset to product | assets + product_assets | XOR: product_id set, product_family_id null |
| Asset to family | assets + product_assets | XOR: product_family_id set, product_id null |
| Multiple assets to product | Batch assets + batch junctions | Sort_order for display order |

---

## DETAILED ASSET WORKFLOWS

### Scenario 1: New Product with Single Image

Most common scenario. Create asset and junction in same transaction.

```json
{
  "goal": "Create asset for new product",
  "operations": [
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "assets",
      "data": {
        "name": "PET Jar 500ml Hero",
        "storage_url": "pending/20241217_studio_abc.png",
        "storage_provider": "SUPABASE",
        "file_name": "20241217_studio_abc.png",
        "asset_type": "IMAGE",
        "status": "ACTIVE",
        "is_ai_generated": true,
        "source_asset_ids": null,
        "generation_prompt": "extraction + white bg + side rake light for honeycomb texture",
        "caption": "500ml PET jar with honeycomb texture"
      },
      "returns": "asset"
    },
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "product_assets",
      "data": {
        "product_id": "@product.id",
        "product_family_id": null,
        "asset_id": "@asset.id",
        "asset_role": "PRIMARY",
        "sort_order": 0
      },
      "dependencies": ["asset", "product"]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Note:** `source_asset_ids` is null when source is from inbox/ (user upload, not yet an asset).

### Scenario 2: New Product with Multiple Images

Multiple angles of same product. Create multiple assets with sort_order.

```json
{
  "goal": "Create product with 4 angle shots",
  "operations": [
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "assets",
      "data": [
        {"name": "Front view", "storage_url": "pending/t/front.png", ...},
        {"name": "Side view", "storage_url": "pending/t/side.png", ...},
        {"name": "Back view", "storage_url": "pending/t/back.png", ...},
        {"name": "Detail view", "storage_url": "pending/t/detail.png", ...}
      ],
      "returns": "assets_batch"
    },
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "product_assets",
      "data": [
        {"product_id": "@product.id", "product_family_id": null, "asset_id": "@assets_batch[0].id", "asset_role": "PRIMARY", "sort_order": 0},
        {"product_id": "@product.id", "product_family_id": null, "asset_id": "@assets_batch[1].id", "asset_role": "GALLERY", "sort_order": 1},
        {"product_id": "@product.id", "product_family_id": null, "asset_id": "@assets_batch[2].id", "asset_role": "GALLERY", "sort_order": 2},
        {"product_id": "@product.id", "product_family_id": null, "asset_id": "@assets_batch[3].id", "asset_role": "ZOOM", "sort_order": 3}
      ],
      "dependencies": ["assets_batch", "product"]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Scenario 3: Variant Set with Individual Images

Each variant gets its own image. Create N assets + N junctions.

```json
{
  "goal": "Create 4 size variants, each with own image",
  "operations": [
    // 4 products already created with returns: "products_batch"
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "assets",
      "data": [
        {"name": "500ml variant", "storage_url": "pending/t/500ml.png", ...},
        {"name": "1L variant", "storage_url": "pending/t/1L.png", ...},
        {"name": "1.5L variant", "storage_url": "pending/t/1_5L.png", ...},
        {"name": "2L variant", "storage_url": "pending/t/2L.png", ...}
      ],
      "returns": "assets_batch"
    },
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "product_assets",
      "data": [
        {"product_id": "@products_batch[0].id", "product_family_id": null, "asset_id": "@assets_batch[0].id", "asset_role": "PRIMARY", "sort_order": 0},
        {"product_id": "@products_batch[1].id", "product_family_id": null, "asset_id": "@assets_batch[1].id", "asset_role": "PRIMARY", "sort_order": 0},
        {"product_id": "@products_batch[2].id", "product_family_id": null, "asset_id": "@assets_batch[2].id", "asset_role": "PRIMARY", "sort_order": 0},
        {"product_id": "@products_batch[3].id", "product_family_id": null, "asset_id": "@assets_batch[3].id", "asset_role": "PRIMARY", "sort_order": 0}
      ],
      "dependencies": ["products_batch", "assets_batch"]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Scenario 4: Family-Level Shared Asset

One lifestyle image shared by all products in family. Link to family, not products.

```json
{
  "goal": "Create family lifestyle image",
  "operations": [
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "assets",
      "data": {
        "name": "PET Storage Family Lifestyle",
        "storage_url": "pending/t/family_lifestyle.png",
        "asset_type": "IMAGE",
        "status": "ACTIVE"
      },
      "returns": "lifestyle_asset"
    },
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "product_assets",
      "data": {
        "product_id": null,
        "product_family_id": "existing-family-uuid",
        "asset_id": "@lifestyle_asset.id",
        "asset_role": "LIFESTYLE",
        "sort_order": 0
      },
      "dependencies": ["lifestyle_asset"]
    }
  ]
}
```

**When to use family-level assets:**
- Lifestyle/contextual shots showing entire product line
- Family size charts
- Shared marketing banners
- Technical diagrams applicable to all variants

### Scenario 5: Add Image to Existing Product

Check if PRIMARY exists before assigning role.

```
FLOW:
1. read_data: Check existing product_assets for this product
2. If PRIMARY exists -> new image is GALLERY
3. If no PRIMARY -> new image is PRIMARY
4. Create asset + junction
```

```json
{
  "goal": "Add secondary image to existing product",
  "reasoning": "Product already has PRIMARY image. Adding as GALLERY.",
  "operations": [
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "assets",
      "data": {"name": "Additional angle", "storage_url": "...", ...},
      "returns": "new_asset"
    },
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "product_assets",
      "data": {
        "product_id": "existing-product-uuid",
        "product_family_id": null,
        "asset_id": "@new_asset.id",
        "asset_role": "GALLERY",
        "sort_order": 1
      },
      "dependencies": ["new_asset"]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Scenario 6: Replace Existing Image

Archive old asset, create new one, update junction.

```json
{
  "goal": "Replace PRIMARY image for product",
  "reasoning": "User requested image replacement. Archiving old, creating new.",
  "operations": [
    {
      "action": "update",
      "table": "assets",
      "filters": {"id": "old-asset-uuid"},
      "updates": {"status": "ARCHIVED"}
    },
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "assets",
      "data": {"name": "Updated hero shot", "storage_url": "...", ...},
      "returns": "new_asset"
    },
    {
      "action": "update",
      "table": "product_assets",
      "filters": {"product_id": "product-uuid", "asset_id": "old-asset-uuid"},
      "updates": {"asset_id": "@new_asset.id"},
      "dependencies": ["new_asset"]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Scenario 7: Multi-Product Image Extraction

One source image contains multiple products. Extract each, create separate assets.

```
SOURCE: Image with 3 different products
OUTPUT: 3 extracted images, 3 assets, 3 junctions

FLOW:
1. visual_analyst identifies 3 distinct products
2. creative_specialist extracts each (3 image_studio calls), creates 3 asset records (HITL for image quality)
3. catalog_specialist creates 3 product_assets junctions (links to existing assets)
```

**creative_specialist creates 3 assets:**
Returns: asset_a_id, asset_b_id, asset_c_id

**catalog_specialist links assets to products:**
```json
{
  "goal": "Link extracted assets to products",
  "reasoning": "3 products extracted by creative_specialist. Assets already created and approved. Now linking to products.",
  "hitl_summary": "Linking 3 extracted images to products.\\n\\n- Product A -> asset_a_id\\n- Product B -> asset_b_id\\n- Product C -> asset_c_id\\n\\nReply *approve* to proceed.",
  "operations": [
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "product_assets",
      "data": [
        {"product_id": "@product_a.id", "asset_id": "asset_a_id", "asset_role": "PRIMARY", "sort_order": 0},
        {"product_id": "@product_b.id", "asset_id": "asset_b_id", "asset_role": "PRIMARY", "sort_order": 0},
        {"product_id": "@product_c.id", "asset_id": "asset_c_id", "asset_role": "PRIMARY", "sort_order": 0}
      ],
      "dependencies": ["product_a", "product_b", "product_c"]
    }
  ],
  "impact": {
    "creates": {"product_assets": 3},
    "warnings": ["Linking pre-approved assets to products"]
  }
}
```

### Scenario 8: Asset Reuse (Link Existing Asset to New Product)

Same asset used for multiple products (e.g., generic accessory image).

```json
{
  "goal": "Link existing cap image to new bottle product",
  "reasoning": "Same cap type used across product line. Reusing existing asset.",
  "operations": [
    {
      "action": "create",
      "table": "product_assets",
      "data": {
        "product_id": "new-product-uuid",
        "product_family_id": null,
        "asset_id": "existing-cap-asset-uuid",
        "asset_role": "GALLERY",
        "sort_order": 5
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**Note:** No new asset created - just a new junction linking existing asset.

---

## COMMON QUERIES

| Query Need | Approach |
|------------|----------|
| Product with its assets | Query products with relations to product_assets, assets |
| Family with assets | Query product_families with relations through product_assets |
| Products with PRIMARY image | Query product_assets filtered by asset_role |
| Products missing images | Query products with product_assets relation, filter empty |

---

## WORKFLOW: IMAGE TO CATALOG

| Stage | Owner | Purpose | Output |
|-------|-------|---------|--------|
| 1. Upload | PM | User sends media | Storage path in inbox/ |
| 2. Visual Analysis | visual_analyst | Assess quality, identify product | Quality assessment |
| 3. Processing | creative_specialist | Background removal, enhancement | Storage path in pending/ |
| 4. Asset Creation | creative_specialist | Create asset record (HITL for image) | asset_id (approved) |
| 5. Catalog Entry | catalog_specialist | Create product + junction (HITL for catalog) | Product linked to asset |

**Two-Stage HITL:**
- Stage 4 HITL: User approves/rejects image quality (creative iterates)
- Stage 5 HITL: User approves/rejects catalog data (catalog iterates)

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Correct Approach |
|--------------|---------|------------------|
| Product without image | Product created but no asset linked | Link asset_id from creative before creating product |
| XOR violation | Both product_id AND product_family_id set | Exactly ONE set, other explicitly null |
| Skip processing | Raw user photo to catalog | Assess quality first, process if needed |
| Invalid storage_url | Empty or incorrect URL | Use actual path from processing output |
| Multiple PRIMARY | Second image assigned PRIMARY | Check existing junctions before role assignment |
| Missing lineage | AI-generated asset without source_asset_ids | Track source for extracted/generated images |
| Family asset for single-product use | Family-level asset when only one product | Use product_id unless truly shared |
| Variant shared image via family | Sharing image across variants using family | Create one asset, multiple product_assets junctions |

### Critical: Asset Ownership (Two-Stage HITL)

**creative_specialist creates assets. catalog_specialist links them to products.**

```
NEW ARCHITECTURE:
1. creative_specialist: create asset (HITL for image quality)
   -> User approves/rejects image -> asset_id returned
2. catalog_specialist: create product + junction (HITL for catalog data)
   -> User approves/rejects catalog data -> product linked

WHY:
- Image feedback goes to image expert (can iterate)
- Catalog feedback goes to catalog expert (can iterate)
- No back-and-forth between specialists for image issues

ORPHAN HANDLING:
- If catalog entry rejected, asset still exists (intentional)
- Asset can be reused or linked to different product
- Standalone assets are valid (e.g., campaign images, user downloads)
```

### STANDALONE Processing (No Asset Record)

**When PM says "Standalone" or "For user download":**

```
FLOW:
1. creative_specialist: process image -> storage_path in pending/
2. Return storage_path to PM (NO write_data, NO asset record)
3. PM shows image to user directly

NO HITL TRIGGERED - image stays as file only, not cataloged.
```

| Signal | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| "Standalone" in delegation | Skip write_data entirely |
| "For user download" | Skip write_data entirely |
| No domain context given | Ask PM for clarification |

**Why STANDALONE exists:**
- Quick image fixes user wants to download immediately
- One-off exports not worth cataloging
- User explicitly doesn't want catalog tracking

**File location:** `pending/` - not moved to approved/ since no asset record.

### Campaign Assets (Temporary Creative Ownership)

**Until campaign_specialist exists, creative_specialist handles campaign_assets junction.**

```
CURRENT ARCHITECTURE:
1. creative_specialist: process campaign images
2. creative_specialist: create asset + campaign_assets junction (single HITL)
3. User approves/rejects campaign creative

FUTURE ARCHITECTURE (when campaign_specialist exists):
1. creative_specialist: create asset (HITL for image quality)
2. campaign_specialist: create campaign_assets junction (HITL for campaign data)
```

| Table | Current Owner | Future Owner |
|-------|---------------|--------------|
| assets | creative_specialist | creative_specialist |
| campaign_assets | creative_specialist | campaign_specialist |

**Why combined for now:**
- No campaign_specialist to own the second stage
- Campaign creative = campaign data (one approval makes sense)
- When campaign_specialist exists, split into Two-Stage pattern

### Critical: Variant Image Decisions

| Scenario | Approach |
|----------|----------|
| Same image for all variants | Create 1 asset + N junctions (one per product) |
| Different image per variant | Create N assets + N junctions |
| Lifestyle for family | Create 1 asset + 1 junction (to product_family_id) |
| Mix: individual + shared | Individual PRIMARY per product, shared LIFESTYLE at family |

---

## ROLE ASSIGNMENT GUIDELINES

| Scenario | Recommended Role |
|----------|------------------|
| First/main product image | PRIMARY |
| Additional product angles | GALLERY |
| Small preview needed | THUMBNAIL |
| Product in lifestyle setting | LIFESTYLE |
| High-res for zoom feature | ZOOM |
| Size/dimension reference | SIZE_CHART |
| Technical specifications | TECHNICAL |
| Compliance certificates | CERTIFICATE |

### Single Product Rule

Each product should have exactly ONE PRIMARY asset. Before assigning PRIMARY role, check if product already has one. If exists, new image should be GALLERY, not PRIMARY.

</protocol>
